-Alan carries no factual developmental biology and says so plainly, twice unprompted. What he has instead is strong architectural intuition: asked how a smooth gradient yields sharp digits, he proposed "a mathematical oscillation combined with some sort of bounding signal" without knowing the field, which is Turing patterning bounded by Hox and FGF — the current best account of digit formation — and also the clock-and-wavefront account of somitogenesis. The gap is vocabulary and cases, not reasoning. He does not hold: morphogen as a named concept, positional information encoded as concentration, maternal determinants, threshold-plus-cross-repression as the general sharpening mechanism, Hox collinearity, or any named model organism result. He reaches for external physics as a symmetry breaker where the answer is usually maternal pre-loading of the oocyte.
+Alan carries no factual developmental biology and says so plainly, but across four probes he reconstructed the field's actual mechanisms from first principles without it, which is a different shape of gap than ignorance. He reached morphogen signalling, Turing patterning bounded by a second signal, epigenetic inheritance through replication, and passive demethylation by breaking the maintenance cycle — four for four, each a real mechanism rather than an analogy for one. What he lacks is vocabulary, named cases and landmark results, not the model. He holds no gene, molecule, organism or experiment by name in this area. Two conceptual gaps remain live: he reaches for external physics as a symmetry breaker where the answer is usually maternal pre-loading of the oocyte, and he treats identity as a mark that persists rather than as a network that continuously re-derives itself, which is why erasure rather than competition was his route to reprogramming.
